From fd2ab4312aca89a654b80851e106c45579219c51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:17:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(backend): RealSense publishers write their
 intrinsics and depth scale

A connected RealSenseRGBDCamera writes its streams' intrinsics (color, depth
sensor, and depth as recorded: aligned to color it has the color intrinsics),
the depth-to-color extrinsics, the depth scale and the device's serial,
firmware and USB type as JSON to <storage>/run/camera-info/<serial>-<output>.json.
Other processes, such as a state snapshot, read them there instead of opening
the camera a second time.

Depth from a device whose depth scale is not 1 mm is converted to millimetres,
which is what the store, datasets and LeRobot expect.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
